SQL queries, database migrations, and input validation schemas.\n- Investigate and fix customer-reported UI and API bugs with guidance during pairing sessions.\n- Add automated integration and component tests alongside every feature pull request.\n- Document endpoints and setup steps so teammates can onboard quickly.\n\nRequirements:\n- Computer science degree, intensive bootcamp, or a strong portfolio of full-stack projects.\n- Working knowledge of JavaScript/TypeScript, React, and Node.js.\n- Comfort writing basic SQL queries and understanding relational tables and foreign keys.\n- Familiarity with Git branching, pull requests, and debugging browser/server logs.\n- Curiosity, coachability, and eagerness to grow through structured code reviews.\n\nNice to have:\n- Exposure to Next.js, Supabase, or Docker in personal or internship projects.\n- Experience deploying an app to Vercel, Railway, or similar cloud platforms.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $700–$1,200 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Private medical insurance and annual dental/vision allowance\n- 20 days paid annual leave plus national public holidays\n- $1,200/year learning, certification, and technical book stipend\n- Company-issued laptop and hybrid workspace equipment budget\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["JavaScript","TypeScript","Node.js","React","PostgreSQL","Git","REST APIs"],"reqs":["Computer science degree, intensive bootcamp, or a strong portfolio of full-stack projects.","Working knowledge of JavaScript/TypeScript, React, and Node.js.","Comfort writing basic SQL queries and understanding relational tables and foreign keys.","Familiarity with Git branching, pull requests, and debugging browser/server logs.","Curiosity, coachability, and eagerness to grow through structured code reviews."],"lo":700,"hi":1200,"days":8,"hours":8},{"company":"Cedar Labs","title":"Mobile Developer (React Native)","description":"Cedar Labs builds web, mobile, and dispatch software for retail and last-mile logistics teams across the Levant and Gulf. Founded by product engineers in Beirut, our 35-person team ships weekly releases directly with store operators and fleet coordinators. We're hiring a Mobile Developer (React Native) to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nOwn key features in our courier driver and store-tablet apps—handling background GPS updates, offline queue sync, barcode scanning, and instant push alerts.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Build and maintain features in our React Native (TypeScript) iOS and Android courier applications.\n- Optimize offline-first data syncing, GPS location tracking, and battery/memory footprint.\n- Monitor crash analytics, diagnose native bridge issues, and keep crash-free sessions above 99.5%.\n- Manage TestFlight, Play Console staged rollouts, and over-the-air updates.\n- Partner closely with product designers and backend engineers to polish driver-facing flows.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years of commercial experience building and shipping React Native applications.\n- At least one published app in the Apple App Store or Google Play Store you can walk us through.\n- Strong TypeScript skills and familiarity with native iOS (Xcode) and Android (Gradle) build tooling.\n- Experience handling REST APIs, offline storage, push notifications, and permissions.\n- Ability to work on-site in Beirut alongside hardware/tablet testing setups.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with Expo EAS Build, Reanimated, or native Swift/Kotlin modules.\n- Background in mapping, geolocation, or logistics apps.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Private medical insurance and annual dental/vision allowance\n- 20 days paid annual leave plus national public holidays\n- $1,200/year learning, certification, and technical book stipend\n- Company-issued laptop and hybrid workspace equipment budget\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["React Native","TypeScript","iOS","Android","REST APIs","Git"],"reqs":["2+ years of commercial experience building and shipping React Native applications.","At least one published app in the Apple App Store or Google Play Store you can walk us through.","Strong TypeScript skills and familiarity with native iOS (Xcode) and Android (Gradle) build tooling.","Experience handling REST APIs, offline storage, push notifications, and permissions.","Ability to work on-site in Beirut alongside hardware/tablet testing setups."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":15,"hours":13},{"company":"Cedar Labs","title":"Software Engineering Intern","description":"Cedar Labs builds web, mobile, and dispatch software for retail and last-mile logistics teams across the Levant and Gulf. Founded by product engineers in Beirut, our 35-person team ships weekly releases directly with store operators and fleet coordinators. We're hiring a Software Engineering Intern to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nA structured 12-week paid internship in Beirut where you pair daily with senior engineers, ship real improvements to internal tools, and present a capstone feature.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Pair with mentors to pick up scoped frontend and API tickets in our staging and production repos.\n- Build and polish internal operations tools used by our customer support and onboarding teams.\n- Write clean, readable code and learn Git workflows, testing, and pull-request etiquette.\n- Join weekly engineering demos and present a final project to the entire product team.\n\nRequirements:\n- Currently pursuing (or recently completed) a degree in computer science, software engineering, or related field.\n- Solid foundation in HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and basic React components.\n- At least one personal, university, or hackathon project hosted on GitHub you can explain.\n- Available on-site in Beirut for at least 3–4 days per week during the internship.\n\nNice to have:\n- Basic exposure to TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, or SQL.\n- Participation in university coding clubs or open-source contributions.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $300–$550 USD / month (Internship, On-site)\n- Private medical insurance and annual dental/vision allowance\n- 20 days paid annual leave plus national public holidays\n- $1,200/year learning, certification, and technical book stipend\n- Company-issued laptop and hybrid workspace equipment budget\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Software","seniority":"intern","type":"internship","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["JavaScript","HTML","CSS","Git","React"],"reqs":["Currently pursuing (or recently completed) a degree in computer science, software engineering, or related field.","Solid foundation in HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and basic React components.","At least one personal, university, or hackathon project hosted on GitHub you can explain.","Available on-site in Beirut for at least 3–4 days per week during the internship."],"lo":300,"hi":550,"days":1,"hours":18},{"company":"Lumen Analytics","title":"Backend Engineer (Node.js)","description":"Lumen Analytics turns fragmented operational and supply-chain data into live forecasting dashboards for mid-market European companies. Our remote-first engineering and data teams serve 140+ B2B customers across logistics, retail, and manufacturing. We're hiring a Backend Engineer (Node.js) to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nArchitect and scale our multi-tenant data ingestion and webhook processing platform that ingests millions of ERP and POS events per day with strict tenant isolation.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Design and build resilient Node.js/TypeScript backend services for high-throughput client data ingestion.\n- Model complex PostgreSQL schemas, optimize slow queries via EXPLAIN ANALYZE, and manage Redis job queues.\n- Own service reliability, structured logging, metrics, and SLO alerting across AWS workloads.\n- Author RFCs for cross-team API contracts and review architecture proposals.\n- Mentor mid-level backend engineers through design reviews and pair debugging.\n\nRequirements:\n- 5+ years of production backend engineering experience, with at least 3 years in Node.js and TypeScript.\n- Deep production expertise with PostgreSQL (indexing, transactions, locking, query tuning) and Redis.\n- Hands-on experience running containerized services on AWS (ECS/EKS, RDS, SQS/S3).\n- Proven track record designing public or internal APIs with versioning, rate limiting, and idempotency.\n- Strong ownership mindset with calm, systematic incident-debugging habits.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience building multi-tenant analytics or ETL pipelines.\n- Familiarity with OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, or event-driven architectures.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- Remote-first setup with a $1,000 home-office hardware grant\n- 28 days paid annual leave and flexible core hours (10:00–15:00 CET overlap)\n- Annual $1,500 personal development and conference budget\n- Annual company-wide offsite and quarterly team meetups\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Node.js","TypeScript","PostgreSQL","Docker","AWS","Redis","System Design"],"reqs":["5+ years of production backend engineering experience, with at least 3 years in Node.js and TypeScript.","Deep production expertise with PostgreSQL (indexing, transactions, locking, query tuning) and Redis.","Hands-on experience running containerized services on AWS (ECS/EKS, RDS, SQS/S3).","Proven track record designing public or internal APIs with versioning, rate limiting, and idempotency.","Strong ownership mindset with calm, systematic incident-debugging habits."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":8,"hours":23},{"company":"Lumen Analytics","title":"Data Analyst","description":"Lumen Analytics turns fragmented operational and supply-chain data into live forecasting dashboards for mid-market European companies. Our remote-first engineering and data teams serve 140+ B2B customers across logistics, retail, and manufacturing. We're hiring a Data Analyst to join the team (hybrid, Berlin, Germany).\n\nAbout the role:\nHelp mid-size retail and logistics clients turn raw ERP exports into clean, trustworthy weekly KPI dashboards and actionable operational analyses.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Write clean, well-documented SQL and Python scripts to clean, validate, and reconcile incoming client datasets.\n- Build interactive Power BI dashboards tracking inventory turns, margin, and delivery SLAs.\n- Investigate data anomalies and partner with engineering to fix upstream ingestion gaps.\n- Prepare clear visual summaries and present findings to non-technical client stakeholders.\n- Maintain a shared metrics dictionary so definitions stay consistent across reports.\n\nRequirements:\n- 1–2 years of experience (or strong academic/project portfolio) in data analysis or BI.\n- Strong SQL fluency (joins, CTEs, window functions, aggregations) and solid Excel skills.\n- Working knowledge of Python (pandas) and at least one BI tool such as Power BI or Tableau.\n- Solid grounding in descriptive statistics and spotting data-quality edge cases.\n- Clear, structured communication skills in English.\n\nNice to have:\n- Exposure to dbt, PostgreSQL, or BigQuery.\n- German language skills for DACH client workshops.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Remote-first setup with a $1,000 home-office hardware grant\n- 28 days paid annual leave and flexible core hours (10:00–15:00 CET overlap)\n- Annual $1,500 personal development and conference budget\n- Annual company-wide offsite and quarterly team meetups\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Berlin, Germany","skills":["SQL","Python","Excel","Power BI","Statistics","Data Visualization"],"reqs":["1–2 years of experience (or strong academic/project portfolio) in data analysis or BI.","Strong SQL fluency (joins, CTEs, window functions, aggregations) and solid Excel skills.","Working knowledge of Python (pandas) and at least one BI tool such as Power BI or Tableau.","Solid grounding in descriptive statistics and spotting data-quality edge cases.","Clear, structured communication skills in English."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":15,"hours":4},{"company":"Lumen Analytics","title":"Machine Learning Engineer","description":"Lumen Analytics turns fragmented operational and supply-chain data into live forecasting dashboards for mid-market European companies. Our remote-first engineering and data teams serve 140+ B2B customers across logistics, retail, and manufacturing. We're hiring a Machine Learning Engineer to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nTake demand-forecasting models and LLM-assisted anomaly explanations from notebook experiments to reliable, monitored production pipelines.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Build, train, and calibrate time-series forecasting models (PyTorch / gradient boosting) for client inventory planning.\n- Design automated evaluation harnesses, backtesting pipelines, and drift monitoring in production.\n- Develop structured LLM workflows (with strict schema validation and guardrails) to summarize forecast drivers.\n- Containerize training and inference jobs with Docker and collaborate with backend teams on low-latency serving.\n- Partner with product managers to separate problems that genuinely benefit from ML from simple heuristics.\n\nRequirements:\n- 4+ years of experience shipping and maintaining machine learning models in production.\n- Strong Python engineering skills, PyTorch or scikit-learn proficiency, and solid SQL.\n- Practical experience with model evaluation, backtesting, feature stores, and experiment tracking.\n- Solid statistical foundation in forecasting, regression, and error analysis.\n- Hands-on experience deploying Dockerized ML services and monitoring latency/accuracy.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with temporal fusion transformers, LightGBM, or hierarchical forecasting.\n- Production experience evaluating and guardrailing LLM outputs.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- Remote-first setup with a $1,000 home-office hardware grant\n- 28 days paid annual leave and flexible core hours (10:00–15:00 CET overlap)\n- Annual $1,500 personal development and conference budget\n- Annual company-wide offsite and quarterly team meetups\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Python","PyTorch","SQL","MLOps","Docker","Statistics","LLMs"],"reqs":["4+ years of experience shipping and maintaining machine learning models in production.","Strong Python engineering skills, PyTorch or scikit-learn proficiency, and solid SQL.","Practical experience with model evaluation, backtesting, feature stores, and experiment tracking.","Solid statistical foundation in forecasting, regression, and error analysis.","Hands-on experience deploying Dockerized ML services and monitoring latency/accuracy."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":1,"hours":9},{"company":"Lumen Analytics","title":"DevOps Engineer","description":"Lumen Analytics turns fragmented operational and supply-chain data into live forecasting dashboards for mid-market European companies. Our remote-first engineering and data teams serve 140+ B2B customers across logistics, retail, and manufacturing. We're hiring a DevOps Engineer to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nStrengthen the cloud foundation behind Lumen's analytics platform—improving Kubernetes reliability, Terraform automation, deployment speed, and observability.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Manage and harden production Kubernetes clusters and RDS databases on AWS using Terraform.\n- Maintain fast, secure GitHub Actions CI/CD pipelines with automated security and image scanning.\n- Expand observability across services using Prometheus, Grafana, and centralized structured logs.\n- Automate backup verification, secrets rotation, and zero-downtime database migration workflows.\n- Participate in blameless post-incident reviews and drive follow-up reliability improvements.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of DevOps, Infrastructure, or SRE experience running production Linux workloads on AWS.\n- Strong hands-on proficiency with Docker, Kubernetes, and Terraform (IaC).\n- Experience building CI/CD pipelines and automating infrastructure deployments.\n- Practical knowledge of networking (VPC, IAM, TLS, DNS) and monitoring/alerting stacks.\n- Clear documentation habits and calm troubleshooting under pressure.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience managing PostgreSQL high availability or Kafka/RabbitMQ on AWS.\n- AWS Solutions Architect or CKA certification.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- Remote-first setup with a $1,000 home-office hardware grant\n- 28 days paid annual leave and flexible core hours (10:00–15:00 CET overlap)\n- Annual $1,500 personal development and conference budget\n- Annual company-wide offsite and quarterly team meetups\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Docker","Kubernetes","Terraform","AWS","CI/CD","Linux","Monitoring"],"reqs":["3+ years of DevOps, Infrastructure, or SRE experience running production Linux workloads on AWS.","Strong hands-on proficiency with Docker, Kubernetes, and Terraform (IaC).","Experience building CI/CD pipelines and automating infrastructure deployments.","Practical knowledge of networking (VPC, IAM, TLS, DNS) and monitoring/alerting stacks.","Clear documentation habits and calm troubleshooting under pressure."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":8,"hours":14},{"company":"Kite Payments","title":"QA Engineer","description":"Kite Payments runs card acquiring, payout orchestration, and fraud screening infrastructure for over 4,000 online merchants across the GCC. Regulated and security-first, we process high-volume multi-currency transactions with sub-second checkout latency. We're hiring a QA Engineer to join the team (hybrid, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nGuard the reliability of our merchant checkout, settlement dashboard, and 3DS authentication flows where every edge case directly impacts real revenue.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Design and maintain automated end-to-end test suites in Playwright covering checkout and merchant portal flows.\n- Build thorough API contract and negative-path test cases for payment, refund, and webhook endpoints.\n- Execute pre-release regression cycles with sandbox payment gateways and edge-case currency/card scenarios.\n- Verify database state and settlement calculations directly via SQL queries.\n- Write clear, reproducible bug reports and pair with developers to root-cause flaky tests.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years of QA engineering experience on web applications and REST APIs.\n- Hands-on proficiency writing automated browser tests in Playwright (or Cypress) using JavaScript/TypeScript.\n- Solid understanding of HTTP status codes, API testing tools (Postman/Insomnia), and SQL.\n- Detail-oriented mindset with experience testing financial, e-commerce, or auth workflows.\n- Comfort working in Git and CI/CD pipelines.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience testing payment gateways, PCI-DSS flows, or webhooks.\n- Familiarity with load testing tools such as k6 or Locust.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Comprehensive UAE medical insurance for employee and dependents\n- Annual flight ticket allowance and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Performance bonus tied to company reliability and growth milestones\n- Relocation support for candidates moving to Dubai\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Testing","Playwright","JavaScript","API Testing","SQL","Git"],"reqs":["2+ years of QA engineering experience on web applications and REST APIs.","Hands-on proficiency writing automated browser tests in Playwright (or Cypress) using JavaScript/TypeScript.","Solid understanding of HTTP status codes, API testing tools (Postman/Insomnia), and SQL.","Detail-oriented mindset with experience testing financial, e-commerce, or auth workflows.","Comfort working in Git and CI/CD pipelines."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":15,"hours":19},{"company":"Kite Payments","title":"Senior Backend Engineer (Payments)","description":"Kite Payments runs card acquiring, payout orchestration, and fraud screening infrastructure for over 4,000 online merchants across the GCC. Regulated and security-first, we process high-volume multi-currency transactions with sub-second checkout latency. We're hiring a Senior Backend Engineer (Payments) to join the team (hybrid, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nBuild and harden the core ledger, settlement, and real-time fraud orchestration engines powering thousands of GCC e-commerce checkouts every minute.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Design and implement idempotent payment processing, ledger posting, and merchant settlement services in Java/Spring Boot.\n- Optimize Kafka event pipelines and PostgreSQL transactions for strict double-entry financial consistency.\n- Reduce p99 fraud-scoring and gateway-routing latency while maintaining PCI-DSS security standards.\n- Lead technical design reviews, threat modeling, and code quality standards across the core payments squad.\n- Support production operations with clear runbooks, circuit breakers, and reconciliation alerts.\n\nRequirements:\n- 5+ years of backend software engineering experience with Java and Spring Boot.\n- Production experience with transactional relational databases (PostgreSQL) and event streaming (Kafka).\n- Strong grasp of distributed systems patterns: idempotency keys, outbox pattern, retries, and concurrency.\n- Experience building high-reliability financial, fintech, or regulated APIs.\n- Security-first engineering mindset (encryption, auth, audit logging).\n\nNice to have:\n- Direct experience with card schemes (Visa/Mastercard), ISO 8583, or regional GCC payment rails (Mada/Apple Pay).\n- Familiarity with PCI-DSS compliance audits.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Comprehensive UAE medical insurance for employee and dependents\n- Annual flight ticket allowance and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Performance bonus tied to company reliability and growth milestones\n- Relocation support for candidates moving to Dubai\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Java","Spring Boot","PostgreSQL","Kafka","System Design","Security"],"reqs":["5+ years of backend software engineering experience with Java and Spring Boot.","Production experience with transactional relational databases (PostgreSQL) and event streaming (Kafka).","Strong grasp of distributed systems patterns: idempotency keys, outbox pattern, retries, and concurrency.","Experience building high-reliability financial, fintech, or regulated APIs.","Security-first engineering mindset (encryption, auth, audit logging)."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":1,"hours":0},{"company":"Kite Payments","title":"Product Manager","description":"Kite Payments runs card acquiring, payout orchestration, and fraud screening infrastructure for over 4,000 online merchants across the GCC. Regulated and security-first, we process high-volume multi-currency transactions with sub-second checkout latency. We're hiring a Product Manager to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nOwn the merchant dashboard, payout scheduling, and dispute-resolution product area—bridging merchant pain points with engineering and compliance teams in Dubai.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Define the quarterly roadmap and success metrics for Kite's merchant onboarding and payout portal.\n- Conduct weekly discovery interviews with e-commerce founders and finance managers across the UAE and KSA.\n- Write crisp product requirement specs with user flows, edge cases, and acceptance criteria.\n- Analyze funnel drop-offs, settlement ticket volume, and feature adoption using SQL and product analytics.\n- Coordinate launches across engineering, risk/compliance, and customer success teams.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of product management experience on B2B SaaS or fintech products.\n- Proven ability to turn qualitative customer interviews and quantitative SQL/analytics data into clear priorities.\n- Strong experience partnering closely with engineers and designers in agile delivery cycles.\n- Excellent structured writing and stakeholder alignment skills.\n\nNice to have:\n- Domain background in payments, checkout conversion, or MENA fintech regulation.\n- Fluency in Arabic alongside English.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive UAE medical insurance for employee and dependents\n- Annual flight ticket allowance and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Performance bonus tied to company reliability and growth milestones\n- Relocation support for candidates moving to Dubai\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Product Management","User Research","Roadmapping","SQL","Communication","Agile"],"reqs":["3+ years of product management experience on B2B SaaS or fintech products.","Proven ability to turn qualitative customer interviews and quantitative SQL/analytics data into clear priorities.","Strong experience partnering closely with engineers and designers in agile delivery cycles.","Excellent structured writing and stakeholder alignment skills."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":8,"hours":5},{"company":"Northwind Studio","title":"Product Designer","description":"Northwind Studio is an independent product design and research studio partnering with seed-to-Series-B startups in Europe and North America. We embed directly with founders to take zero-to-one products from discovery interviews to shipped design systems. We're hiring a Product Designer to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead end-to-end product design for two early-stage startup engagements at a time—shaping product strategy, interaction flows, and production-ready Figma systems.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Own discovery through visual polish for web and mobile SaaS products across our client roster.\n- Run user interviews and moderated usability tests, synthesizing findings into actionable flow improvements.\n- Build interactive Figma prototypes to align founders and validate complex workflows before engineering starts.\n- Create and maintain scalable component libraries with tokens, states, and clear developer handoff notes.\n- Present design rationales directly to startup founders and iterate rapidly on feedback.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of product design experience shipping B2B or consumer web/mobile applications.\n- A strong portfolio demonstrating end-to-end problem solving—from research and IA to final UI craft.\n- Expert proficiency in Figma (auto-layout, variables/tokens, interactive prototyping).\n- Comfort running usability tests and communicating clearly in async remote environments.\n\nNice to have:\n- Working knowledge of HTML/CSS/Tailwind constraints or Framer Motion prototyping.\n- Experience working in a design agency or early-stage startup.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- 100% remote async-friendly culture with 4-day summer Fridays\n- 25 days paid leave plus end-of-year studio closure\n- $1,000/year Figma, research tools, and design conference stipend\n- Monthly wellness and coworking pass reimbursement\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Design","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Figma","UX Design","UI Design","Prototyping","User Research","Design Systems"],"reqs":["3+ years of product design experience shipping B2B or consumer web/mobile applications.","A strong portfolio demonstrating end-to-end problem solving—from research and IA to final UI craft.","Expert proficiency in Figma (auto-layout, variables/tokens, interactive prototyping).","Comfort running usability tests and communicating clearly in async remote environments."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":15,"hours":10},{"company":"Northwind Studio","title":"Junior UI Designer","description":"Northwind Studio is an independent product design and research studio partnering with seed-to-Series-B startups in Europe and North America. We embed directly with founders to take zero-to-one products from discovery interviews to shipped design systems. We're hiring a Junior UI Designer to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nCollaborate with senior product designers on visual exploration, responsive screens, component variants, and crisp design-to-dev handoff across client apps.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Design clean, responsive web and mobile screens building on established wireframes and design systems.\n- Explore typography, color, and layout directions for landing pages and onboarding flows.\n- Maintain tidy Figma component libraries with proper naming, states (hover, error, empty), and responsive breakpoints.\n- Prepare developer-ready specs and participate in design QA on staging builds.\n- Join weekly studio critiques to share work-in-progress and sharpen visual taste.\n\nRequirements:\n- A curated portfolio showcasing strong visual craft, typography, spacing, and UI hierarchy.\n- 1+ year of experience (or standout internship/freelance work) designing digital interfaces in Figma.\n- Strong attention to detail across alignment, contrast, and micro-copy.\n- Openness to constructive critique and collaborative iteration in a remote team.\n\nNice to have:\n- Basic illustration, custom icon design, or motion prototyping skills.\n- Understanding of WCAG color contrast and accessibility basics.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- 100% remote async-friendly culture with 4-day summer Fridays\n- 25 days paid leave plus end-of-year studio closure\n- $1,000/year Figma, research tools, and design conference stipend\n- Monthly wellness and coworking pass reimbursement\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Design","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Figma","UI Design","Typography","Prototyping","Design Systems"],"reqs":["A curated portfolio showcasing strong visual craft, typography, spacing, and UI hierarchy.","1+ year of experience (or standout internship/freelance work) designing digital interfaces in Figma.","Strong attention to detail across alignment, contrast, and micro-copy.","Openness to constructive critique and collaborative iteration in a remote team."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":1,"hours":15},{"company":"Northwind Studio","title":"UX Researcher","description":"Northwind Studio is an independent product design and research studio partnering with seed-to-Series-B startups in Europe and North America. We embed directly with founders to take zero-to-one products from discovery interviews to shipped design systems. We're hiring an UX Researcher to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead foundational discovery and evaluative usability studies on 4–8 week client sprints so startup teams build the right product before committing engineering quarters.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Scope, plan, and execute qualitative discovery interviews and unmoderated/moderated usability studies.\n- Design screener surveys, recruit niche B2B/consumer participants, and manage research ethics/consent.\n- Synthesize sessions into crisp decision-ready insights, journey maps, and prioritized product recommendations.\n- Partner with product designers to test prototypes and validate riskiest product assumptions.\n- Coach client founders on lightweight continuous research habits they can sustain post-engagement.\n\nRequirements:\n- 5+ years of dedicated UX research experience across mixed qualitative and quantitative methods.\n- Clear case studies showing how your research directly changed a product direction or metric.\n- Strong moderation skills—able to run unbiased interviews and uncover root behaviors.\n- Ability to work independently on remote contract sprints with fast turnaround.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with Dovetail, Maze, UserTesting, or quantitative product analytics.\n- Background researching fintech, developer tools, or healthcare products.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Contract, Remote)\n- 100% remote async-friendly culture with 4-day summer Fridays\n- 25 days paid leave plus end-of-year studio closure\n- $1,000/year Figma, research tools, and design conference stipend\n- Monthly wellness and coworking pass reimbursement\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Design","seniority":"senior","type":"contract","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["User Research","Usability Testing","Interviewing","Survey Design","Synthesis"],"reqs":["5+ years of dedicated UX research experience across mixed qualitative and quantitative methods.","Clear case studies showing how your research directly changed a product direction or metric.","Strong moderation skills—able to run unbiased interviews and uncover root behaviors.","Ability to work independently on remote contract sprints with fast turnaround."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":8,"hours":20},{"company":"Northwind Studio","title":"Design Intern","description":"Northwind Studio is an independent product design and research studio partnering with seed-to-Series-B startups in Europe and North America. We embed directly with founders to take zero-to-one products from discovery interviews to shipped design systems. We're hiring a Design Intern to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nA 12-week mentored remote internship shadowing senior designers on real client sprints, crafting UI components, icons, and interactive Figma prototypes.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Assist senior designers in building UI screens, component states, and responsive tablet/mobile variants.\n- Create custom spot illustrations, empty-state graphics, and clean marketing visuals.\n- Help organize Figma files, take notes during user interviews, and assemble usability test clips.\n- Participate in twice-weekly design critiques and complete a mentored portfolio case study.\n\nRequirements:\n- Currently studying graphic/product design, HCI, or building an independent design portfolio.\n- Familiarity with Figma frames, components, and basic prototyping.\n- A small portfolio (2–4 class or personal projects) showing thoughtful layout and curiosity.\n- Reliable internet connection and strong English communication for remote collaboration.\n\nNice to have:\n- Interest in motion design, micro-interactions, or front-end CSS.\n- Experience designing for dark/light themes or design tokens.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $450–$800 USD / month (Internship, Remote)\n- 100% remote async-friendly culture with 4-day summer Fridays\n- 25 days paid leave plus end-of-year studio closure\n- $1,000/year Figma, research tools, and design conference stipend\n- Monthly wellness and coworking pass reimbursement\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Design","seniority":"intern","type":"internship","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Figma","UI Design","Illustration","Prototyping"],"reqs":["Currently studying graphic/product design, HCI, or building an independent design portfolio.","Familiarity with Figma frames, components, and basic prototyping.","A small portfolio (2–4 class or personal projects) showing thoughtful layout and curiosity.","Reliable internet connection and strong English communication for remote collaboration."],"lo":450,"hi":800,"days":15,"hours":1},{"company":"Olive & Co","title":"Graphic Designer","description":"Olive & Co is a creative brand and performance growth agency helping consumer, F&B, and lifestyle brands scale across the MENA region. Our strategists, designers, and media buyers manage end-to-end launches from identity to paid acquisition. We're hiring a Graphic Designer to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nShape cohesive brand identities, campaign key visuals, packaging concepts, and social toolkits for ambitious consumer and F&B brands across Dubai and the GCC.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Develop brand identity systems—logos, bilingual typography pairings, color palettes, and usage guidelines.\n- Design high-impact campaign key visuals for OOH, print collateral, retail displays, and digital ads.\n- Prepare print-ready mechanical files with accurate bleeds, dielines, and color profiles.\n- Collaborate with copywriters and motion designers on seasonal product launches.\n- Present creative concepts confidently to clients and incorporate feedback constructively.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of graphic/brand design experience in a creative agency or in-house consumer brand.\n- Strong portfolio highlighting brand identity systems, editorial layouts, and campaign visuals.\n- Expert proficiency in Adobe Illustrator, Photoshop, InDesign, and Figma.\n- Solid understanding of grid systems, typography hierarchy, and print production specs.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with Arabic typography and bilingual English–Arabic brand layouts.\n- Packaging design or 3D mockup rendering skills (Blender/Dimension).\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive health insurance and 21 days paid annual leave\n- Creative software subscriptions and portfolio production support\n- Quarterly team showcases and annual performance bonus\n- Flexible Thursday afternoon finish during non-campaign weeks\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Design","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Adobe Illustrator","Adobe Photoshop","Branding","Typography","Layout","Figma"],"reqs":["3+ years of graphic/brand design experience in a creative agency or in-house consumer brand.","Strong portfolio highlighting brand identity systems, editorial layouts, and campaign visuals.","Expert proficiency in Adobe Illustrator, Photoshop, InDesign, and Figma.","Solid understanding of grid systems, typography hierarchy, and print production specs."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":1,"hours":6},{"company":"Olive & Co","title":"Motion Designer","description":"Olive & Co is a creative brand and performance growth agency helping consumer, F&B, and lifestyle brands scale across the MENA region. Our strategists, designers, and media buyers manage end-to-end launches from identity to paid acquisition. We're hiring a Motion Designer to join the team (hybrid, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nBring client campaigns to life with kinetic typography, product launch reels, paid-social motion ads, and modular After Effects templates.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Storyboard and animate 2D/2.5D motion graphics, kinetic type reels, and social performance ads in After Effects.\n- Edit short-form launch films and UGC-style brand stories tailored for Reels, TikTok, and YouTube Shorts.\n- Build reusable MOGRT / After Effects templates so the social team can localize campaign variations quickly.\n- Ensure smooth pacing, sound design sync, and crisp visual alignment with client brand guidelines.\n- Deliver multiple aspect ratios (9:16, 4:5, 16:9) reliably within tight campaign timelines.\n\nRequirements:\n- A standout motion reel showing commercial brand, social ad, or kinetic typography work.\n- 2+ years of experience in After Effects, Premiere Pro, and Illustrator/Photoshop.\n- Strong sense of timing, easing curves, sound pacing, and visual storytelling.\n- Ability to balance multiple client revisions cleanly under agency campaign deadlines.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with Lottie/Rive web animations or Cinema 4D / Blender.\n- Arabic/English bilingual kinetic typography experience.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Contract, Hybrid)\n- Comprehensive health insurance and 21 days paid annual leave\n- Creative software subscriptions and portfolio production support\n- Quarterly team showcases and annual performance bonus\n- Flexible Thursday afternoon finish during non-campaign weeks\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Design","seniority":"mid","type":"contract","mode":"hybrid","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["After Effects","Motion Design","Video Editing","Illustrator","Storyboarding"],"reqs":["A standout motion reel showing commercial brand, social ad, or kinetic typography work.","2+ years of experience in After Effects, Premiere Pro, and Illustrator/Photoshop.","Strong sense of timing, easing curves, sound pacing, and visual storytelling.","Ability to balance multiple client revisions cleanly under agency campaign deadlines."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":8,"hours":11},{"company":"Olive & Co","title":"Digital Marketing Specialist","description":"Olive & Co is a creative brand and performance growth agency helping consumer, F&B, and lifestyle brands scale across the MENA region. Our strategists, designers, and media buyers manage end-to-end launches from identity to paid acquisition. We're hiring a Digital Marketing Specialist to join the team (hybrid, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nManage paid acquisition budgets and conversion experiments for 5–7 fast-moving consumer e-commerce and hospitality clients across the Gulf.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Plan, launch, and optimize full-funnel Meta, Google Search/Shopping, and TikTok paid campaigns.\n- Structure weekly creative and landing-page A/B tests to lower CAC and lift ROAS.\n- Audit conversion tracking (GA4, Meta Pixel/CAPI, Google Tag Manager) to ensure clean attribution.\n- Deliver clear Monday performance recaps to clients with concrete next-week budget recommendations.\n- Collaborate with copywriters and motion designers on high-converting ad hooks.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years managing paid social and search campaigns with measurable revenue or lead-gen targets.\n- Proven case studies showing ROAS, CPA, or CTR improvements you drove directly.\n- Hands-on proficiency with Meta Ads Manager, Google Ads, GA4, and Tag Manager.\n- Analytical rigor with spreadsheets and clear client-facing reporting.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience scaling Shopify or WooCommerce e-commerce brands in the GCC.\n- Google Ads or Meta Blueprint certifications.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Comprehensive health insurance and 21 days paid annual leave\n- Creative software subscriptions and portfolio production support\n- Quarterly team showcases and annual performance bonus\n- Flexible Thursday afternoon finish during non-campaign weeks\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Marketing","s