mpetency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Marketing","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Brand Management","Marketing Strategy","Budgeting","Team Leadership","Analytics","Campaign Management"],"reqs":["6+ years in consumer, F&B, retail, or delivery-app marketing.","2+ years directly managing a multidisciplinary marketing team and owning budgets.","Track record running integrated online + offline campaigns that lifted store footfall and app orders.","Strong analytical comfort alongside sharp creative and brand judgment."],"lo":2400,"hi":3800,"days":15,"hours":7},{"company":"Saffron Kitchens","title":"Growth Marketing Analyst","description":"Saffron Kitchens operates 18 neighborhood restaurants alongside a high-volume direct delivery app serving 25,000+ weekly orders. We combine hospitality craft with modern kitchen operations, CRM retention, and real-time order logistics. We're hiring a Growth Marketing Analyst to join the team (hybrid, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nTurn app ordering, promo code, and customer retention data into clear experiments that increase repeat orders and lower delivery acquisition cost.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Analyze customer cohorts, checkout funnel drop-offs, and promo-code ROI using SQL and Excel.\n- Set up and evaluate A/B tests on push notifications, SMS offers, and delivery-fee thresholds.\n- Segment CRM audiences (new, at-risk, VIP diners) to improve lifecycle campaign conversion.\n- Maintain weekly growth scorecards for marketing and operations leadership.\n- Audit event tracking across our web and mobile ordering apps.\n\nRequirements:\n- 1+ year in a marketing analytics, growth, or business intelligence role.\n- Solid SQL and Excel skills (pivot tables, cohort tables, statistical significance checks).\n- Experience with Google Analytics / Mixpanel / Amplitude or CRM campaign tools.\n- Ability to turn raw 