nd updating Canva templates.\n- Coordinate printed POS materials and promo signage with store managers ahead of launches.\n- Compile weekly customer review trends and competitor menu/promo research.\n- Support on-site sampling activations and community events.\n\nRequirements:\n- Currently studying marketing, communications, business, or a related field (or recent graduate).\n- Strong organizational habits, reliable follow-through, and enthusiasm for consumer brands.\n- Basic comfort with Canva and writing short, engaging captions in English and Arabic.\n- Available on-site in Beirut with occasional visits to restaurant branches.\n\nNice to have:\n- Portfolio of university projects, club events, or personal social content.\n- Basic smartphone photography or CapCut editing skills.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $300–$550 USD / month (Internship, On-site)\n- Medical coverage and daily staff meal allowance across all locations\n- 18 days paid annual leave plus paid sick and family leave\n- Monthly dining credit across all Saffron Kitchens brands\n- Structured career progression across corporate and store leadership\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Marketing","seniority":"intern","type":"internship","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Social Media","Canva","Copywriting","Research"],"reqs":["Currently studying marketing, communications, business, or a related field (or recent graduate).","Strong organizational habits, reliable follow-through, and enthusiasm for consumer brands.","Basic comfort with Canva and writing short, engaging captions in English and Arabic.","Available on-site in Beirut with occasional visits to restaurant branches."],"lo":300,"hi":550,"days":8,"hours":17},{"company":"Saffron Kitchens","title"