 on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Marketing","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Customer Service","CRM","Team Leadership","Process Improvement","Communication"],"reqs":["3+ years in customer experience or support operations, including 1+ year leading a team.","Hands-on experience with CRM/helpdesk platforms (Zendesk, Intercom, Freshdesk, or similar).","Fluency in Arabic and English with calm, empathetic written and spoken communication.","Data-driven approach to SLA tracking and root-cause operational fixes."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":15,"hours":22},{"company":"Harbor Finance","title":"Junior Accountant","description":"Harbor Finance provides fractional CFO advisory, statutory audit, tax structuring, and cross-border accounting for high-growth SMEs in the UK and Europe. Our advisory squads combine chartered accountants with modern cloud finance tooling. We're hiring a Junior Accountant to join the team (hybrid, London, UK).\n\nAbout the role:\nManage monthly bookkeeping, multi-currency bank reconciliations, and month-end schedules for a portfolio of fast-growing UK tech and service SMEs.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Process accounts payable/receivable, expense coding, and journal entries in Xero and QuickBooks.\n- Complete weekly and monthly bank, credit-card, and intercompany reconciliations.\n- Prepare VAT return workpapers, fixed-asset schedules, and accruals for month-end close.\n- Respond promptly to client queries regarding invoices, receipts, and supplier balances.\n- Support senior accountants and external auditors during year-end statutory accounts preparation.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in accounting, finance, or economics (or AAT Level 3/4).\n- Working knowledge of double-entry bookkeeping and UK GAAP / IFRS fundamentals.\n- 