–C client companies.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Build and maintain dynamic 3-statement financial models, cash-runway scenarios, and annual budgets.\n- Perform monthly budget-vs-actual variance analyses and translate drivers into clear commentary.\n- Model pricing changes, hiring plans, and working-capital sensitivities ahead of board decisions.\n- Automate management KPI reporting packs using Excel and Power BI.\n- Join monthly client CFO calls to walk founders and finance leads through key financial insights.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of experience in FP&A, financial advisory, transaction services, or corporate finance.\n- Expert financial modeling skills in Excel (integrated P&L, balance sheet, cash flow, scenario switches).\n- Strong accounting fluency and ability to spot anomalies in raw trial balances.\n- Clear executive storytelling—able to turn complex spreadsheets into crisp board slides.\n\nNice to have:\n- ACA/ACCA/CFA progress or completion.\n- Experience modeling SaaS metrics (ARR, NRR, CAC payback) or e-commerce cohorts.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Full study support and paid exam leave for ACCA, ACA, or CPA\n- 25 days paid holiday plus UK bank holidays and hybrid travel card\n- Private medical and dental cover plus pension matching\n- Flexible hybrid schedule (2–3 days/week in our London Bridge office)\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Finance","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"London, UK","skills":["Financial Modeling","Excel","Forecasting","Power BI","Accounting","Presentation"],"reqs":["3+ years of experience in FP&A, financial advisory, transaction services, or corporate finance.","Expert financial modeling skills in Excel (integrated P&L, ba