 UK bank holidays and hybrid travel card\n- Private medical and dental cover plus pension matching\n- Flexible hybrid schedule (2–3 days/week in our London Bridge office)\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Finance","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"London, UK","skills":["Audit","IFRS","Risk Assessment","Excel","Team Leadership","Internal Controls"],"reqs":["Qualified ACA, ACCA, or CPA (or recognized equivalent).","5+ years of external audit experience in an accounting firm, with 2+ years acting as Audit In-Charge/Senior.","Strong technical command of IFRS, FRS 102, and audit sampling/documentation standards.","Proven ability to review junior staff work and deliver engagements on schedule."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":15,"hours":13},{"company":"Harbor Finance","title":"Payroll Specialist","description":"Harbor Finance provides fractional CFO advisory, statutory audit, tax structuring, and cross-border accounting for high-growth SMEs in the UK and Europe. Our advisory squads combine chartered accountants with modern cloud finance tooling. We're hiring a Payroll Specialist to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nRun accurate, compliant monthly UK payroll cycles (25 hrs/week remote) across a portfolio of 20+ SME clients with varying commission and pension setups.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Process end-to-end monthly PAYE payroll runs, starters/leavers, statutory sick/parental pay, and pension auto-enrolment.\n- Verify timesheets, variable bonuses, and benefits-in-kind inputs from client HR contacts.\n- Submit RTI filings (FPS/EPS) to HMRC accurately and on schedule.\n- Prepare payroll journal entries, BACS payment files, and month-end reconciliation summaries.\n- Answer client and employee payslip or tax-code queries politely and promptly.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years running multi-client or multi-entity UK payroll end to end.\n- Solid command of HMRC PAYE, NI, statutory payments, and workplace pension compliance.\n- Hands-on experience with cloud payroll software (BrightPay, PayFit, Xero Payroll, or Sage) and Excel.\n- Exceptionally high accuracy and discretion with sensitive compensation data.\n\nNice to have:\n- CIPP qualification or experience in a payroll bureau/accounting practice.\n- Familiarity with P11D reporting.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,200–$2,000 USD / month (Part-time, Remote)\n- Full study support and paid exam leave for ACCA, ACA, or CPA\n- 25 days paid holiday plus UK bank holidays and hybrid travel card\n- Private medical and dental cover plus pension matching\n- Flexible hybrid schedule (2–3 days/week in our London Bridge office)\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Finance","seniority":"mid","type":"part_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Payroll","Excel","HR Systems","Compliance","Attention to Detail"],"reqs":["2+ years running multi-client or multi-entity UK payroll end to end.","Solid command of HMRC PAYE, NI, statutory payments, and workplace pension compliance.","Hands-on experience with cloud payroll software (BrightPay, PayFit, Xero Payroll, or Sage) and Excel.","Exceptionally high accuracy and discretion with sensitive compensation data."],"lo":1200,"hi":2000,"days":1,"hours":18},{"company":"Kite Payments","title":"Risk & Compliance Analyst","description":"Kite Payments runs card acquiring, payout orchestration, and fraud screening infrastructure for over 4,000 online merchants across the GCC. Regulated and security-first, we process high-volume multi-currency transactions with sub-second checkout latency. We're hiring a Risk & Compliance Analyst to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nProtect Kite's payment ecosystem by reviewing merchant KYB/KYC onboarding files, monitoring live transaction alerts, and supporting Central Bank reporting.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct enhanced due diligence (EDD), UBO verification, and sanctions screening for onboarding merchants.\n- Investigate flagged transaction patterns, chargeback spikes, and potential money-laundering typologies.\n- Document clear case decisions and escalate suspicious activity reports (SARs/STRs) per UAE regulatory rules.\n- Collaborate with sales and onboarding teams to balance fraud protection with fast merchant approval times.\n- Maintain audit-ready compliance logs and support quarterly internal risk assessments.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years in AML/KYC, merchant underwriting, or compliance at a bank, PSP, or fintech.\n- Solid working knowledge of AML/CFT regulations, sanctions lists, and merchant risk indicators.\n- Strong investigative rigor with Excel and case-management systems.\n- Clear, concise written English for regulatory case narratives.\n\nNice to have:\n- ACAMS / ICA certification or experience with UAE Central Bank / DFSA frameworks.\n- Arabic language skills for reviewing regional commercial licenses.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive UAE medical insurance for employee and dependents\n- Annual flight ticket allowance and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Performance bonus tied to company reliability and growth milestones\n- Relocation support for candidates moving to Dubai\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Finance","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","ski