nts\n- Annual flight ticket allowance and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Performance bonus tied to company reliability and growth milestones\n- Relocation support for candidates moving to Dubai\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Finance","seniority":"intern","type":"internship","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Excel","Accounting","Research","Reporting"],"reqs":["Currently studying finance, accounting, economics, or business administration (or recent graduate).","Strong comfort with Excel formulas, pivot tables, and structured spreadsheets.","High attention to detail and eagerness to learn fintech accounting operations.","Available full-time on-site in Dubai for 3–6 months."],"lo":450,"hi":800,"days":15,"hours":4},{"company":"Mediterra Health","title":"Registered Nurse","description":"Mediterra Health operates three multidisciplinary outpatient clinics, an accredited diagnostic lab, and a 24/7 bilingual telehealth platform. Over 80 clinicians collaborate across primary care, chronic disease management, and preventive screenings. We're hiring a Registered Nurse to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nDeliver attentive outpatient triage, clinical procedures, and patient education across our busy multidisciplinary medical center in Beirut.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Perform patient intake assessments, vital signs, triage, and pre-consultation clinical preparation.\n- Administer IV/IM medications, vaccinations, wound dressings, and routine clinical procedures safely.\n- Document clinical observations, care plans, and medication logs accurately in our EMR system.\n- Educate patients and families clearly on post-visit care, chronic disease monitoring, and medication schedules.\n- Maintain strict infection-control standards and emergency crash-cart readiness.\n\nRequirements:\n- BSN / Bachelor of Science in Nursing and an active Lebanese Ministry of Public Health nursing license.\n- 2+ years of clinical nursing experience in an outpatient clinic or hospital setting.\n- Current BLS certification and strong clinical assessment & venipuncture skills.\n- Fluent Arabic and English (French is a strong advantage) with compassionate bedside manner.\n\nNice to have:\n- ACLS certification or experience in pediatrics, cardiology, or chronic care management.\n- Prior experience with modern electronic medical record (EMR) workflows.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive medical coverage and discounted family care at all clinics\n- Paid CME (Continuing Medical Education) days and conference support\n- Malpractice coverage and structured shift scheduling without surprise double-shifts\n- 20 days paid annual leave plus public holidays\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Patient Care","Clinical Assessment","Medication Administration","EMR","Communication"],"reqs":["BSN / Bachelor of Science in Nursing and an active Lebanese Ministry of Public Health nursing license.","2+ years of clinical nursing experience in an outpatient clinic or hospital setting.","Current BLS certification and strong clinical assessment & venipuncture skills.","Fluent Arabic and English (French is a strong advantage) with compassionate bedside manner."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":1,"hours":9},{"company":"Mediterra Health","title":"Telehealth Coordinator","description":"Mediterra Health operates three multidisciplinary outpatient clinics, an accredited diagnostic lab, and a 24/7 bilingual telehealth platform. Over 80 clinicians collaborate across primary care, chronic disease management, and preventive screenings. We're hiring a Telehealth Coordinator to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nServe as the warm, organized first point of contact for virtual care patients—managing video consultations, pre-visit prep, lab follow-ups, and specialist referrals.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Schedule, confirm, and reschedule telehealth appointments across general practice and specialist clinics.\n- Guide patients through joining video calls, uploading prior lab/imaging results, and completing intake forms.\n- Coordinate post-consultation lab bookings, e-prescriptions, and follow-up reminders in the EMR.\n- Monitor the live telehealth queue to keep doctor schedules running smoothly and minimize wait times.\n- Handle patient inquiries with empathy, discretion, and strict privacy compliance.\n\nRequirements:\n- 1+ year of experience in patient coordination, medical reception, or high-empathy customer support.\n- Fluent spoken and written Arabic and English.\n- Comfortable navigating scheduling/EMR software, video tools, and multi-channel messaging.\n- Calm, organized communication style and quiet remote workspace.\n\nNice to have:\n- French language fluency.\n- Prior experience in a clinic, hospital call center, or digital health startup.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $700–$1,200 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- Comprehensive medical coverage and discounted family care at all clinics\n- Paid CME (Continuing Medical Education) days and conference support\n- Malpractice coverage and structured shift scheduling without surprise double-shifts\n- 20 days paid annual leave plus public holidays\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Scheduling","Customer Service","EMR","Communication","Arabic","English"],"reqs":["1+ year of experience in patient coordination, medical reception, or high-empathy customer support.","Fluent spoken and written Arabic and English.","Comfortable navigating scheduling/EMR software, video tools, and multi-channel messaging.","Calm, organized communication style and quiet remote workspace."],"lo":700,"hi":1200,"days":8,"hours":14},{"company":"Mediterra Health","title":"Medical Laboratory Technician","description":"Mediterra Health operates three multidisciplinary outpatient clinics, an accredited diagnostic lab, and a 24/7 bilingual telehealth platform. Over 80 clinicians collaborate across primary care, chronic disease management, and preventive screenings. We're hiring a Medical Laboratory Technician to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nExecute accurate hematology, biochemistry, and microbiology diagnostics inside Mediterra's CAP-aligned outpatient clinical laboratory.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Process blood, urine, and swab specimens from reception through centrifugation, aliquoting, and analysis.\n- Operate and run daily quality-control checks on automated hematology and chemistry analyzers.\n- Validate and enter test results into the LIS/EMR, flagging critical values immediately to physicians.\n- Perform routine instrument calibration, preventive maintenance, and reagent inventory tracking.\n- Adhere strictly to biosafety protocols, PPE standards, and biomedical waste disposal procedures.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Medical Laboratory Science (or licensed Clinical Laboratory Technician).\n- Active practice license and strong grounding in clinical chemistry, hematology, and phlebotomy.\n- Meticulous attention to specimen labeling, QC logs, and turnaround-time targets.\n- Ability to work rotating morning/afternoon clinic shifts cleanly.\n\nNice to have:\n- 1+ year of experience in an accredited hospital or diagnostic lab.\n- Experience with Sysmex, Roche Cobas, or Abbott analyzers.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $700–$1,200 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive medical coverage and discounted family care at all clinics\n- Paid CME (Continuing Medical Education) days and conference support\n- Malpractice coverage and structured shift scheduling without surprise double-shifts\n- 20 days paid annual leave plus public holidays\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Laboratory Testing","Quality Control","Sample Handling","Lab Safety","Attention to Detail"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Medical Laboratory Science (or licensed Clinical Laboratory Technician).","Active practice license and strong grounding in clinical chemistry, hematology, and phlebotomy.","Meticulous attention to specimen labeling, QC logs, and turnaround-time targets.","Ability to work rotating morning/afternoon clinic shifts cleanly."],"lo":700,"hi":1200,"days":15,"hours":19},{"company":"Mediterra Health","title":"Clinic Operations Manager","description":"Mediterra Health operates three multidisciplinary outpatient clinics, an accredited diagnostic lab, and a 24/7 bilingual telehealth platform. Over 80 clinicians collaborate across primary care, chronic disease management, and preventive screenings. We're hiring a Clinic Operations Manager to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nOversee daily non-clinical operations across our flagship Beirut clinic—patient flow, front-desk/nursing staffing, vendor contracts, and service quality.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Manage daily clinic operations, patient throughput, and scheduling efficiency across 18 consultation rooms.\n- Lead and mentor reception, patient-coordination, and facility support teams (20+ staff).\n- Own clinic operating budgets, medical supply procurement, and insurance/TPA billing coordination.\n- Track wait times, appointment utilization, and patient satisfaction (NPS) to eliminate bottlenecks.\n- Ensure ongoing compliance with Ministry of Public Health licensing, safety, and privacy standards.\n\nRequirements:\n- 5+ years in healthcare operations or clinic/hospital administration, with 2+ years managing teams.\n- Track record improving patient wait times, clinic capacity, or billing accuracy.\n- Strong financial literacy (budgeting, vendor negotiation, KPI reporting) and EMR familiarity.\n- Fluent Arabic and English with decisive, people-first leadership.\n\nNice to have:\n- Master's in Healthcare Administration (MHA) or MBA.\n- Experience scaling multi-site outpatient or telehealth operations.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,400–$3,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive medical coverage and discounted family care at all clinics\n- Paid CME (Continuing Medical Education) days and conference support\n- Malpractice coverage and structured shift scheduling without surprise double-shifts\n- 20 days paid annual leave plus public holidays\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Operations Management","Team Leadership","Budgeting","Process Improvement","Healthcare Administration"],"reqs":["5+ years in healthcare operations or clinic/hospital administration, with 2+ years managing teams.","Track record improving patient wait times, clinic capacity, or billing accuracy.","Strong financial literacy (budgeting, vendor negotiation, KPI reporting) and EMR familiarity.","Fluent Arabic and English with decisive, people-first leadership."],"lo":2400,"hi":3800,"days":1,"hours":0},{"company":"Pinewood Clinics","title":"Physiotherapist","description":"Pinewood Clinics is a network of six community family-medicine, physiotherapy, and pharmacy clinics across Île-de-France. We focus on coordinated, unhurried outpatient care backed by shared electronic medical records. We're hiring a Physiotherapist to join the team (on-site, Paris, France).\n\nAbout the role:\nProvide evidence-based musculoskeletal and post-surgical rehabilitation in 45-minute one-on-one sessions at our modern Paris clinics.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct thorough initial biomechanical assessments and set realistic functional recovery milestones.\n- Deliver manual therapy, targeted therapeutic exercise, and mobility/strength progressions.\n- Design clear home-exercise programs and educate patients on injury prevention and posture.\n- Collaborate closely with Pinewood's family doctors and orthopedic partners on shared care plans.\n- Maintain structured progress notes in our shared EMR after each session.\n\nRequirements:\n- French Diplôme d'État de Masseur-Kinésithérapeute and active Ordre registration.\n- 2+ years of outpatient musculoskeletal or sports rehabilitation experience.\n- Fluent French and conversational English for Paris's international patient base.\n- Empathetic, patient-centered communication and collaborative clinical mindset.\n\nNice to have:\n- Additional training in dry needling, sports rehab, or pelvic-floor physiotherapy.\n- Experience with exercise-prescription apps such as Physitrack.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Mutuelle health coverage and 50% Navigo transit pass reimbursement\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus RTT days per French labor standards\n- Meal vouchers (Tickets Restaurant) and annual clinical training budget\n- Modern, well-equipped treatment rooms with dedicated admin support\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Paris, France","skills":["Physiotherapy","Rehabilitation","Patient Assessment","Exercise Therapy","Communication"],"reqs":["French Diplôme d'État de Masseur-Kinésithérapeute and active Ordre registration.","2+ years of outpatient musculoskeletal or sports rehabilitation experience.","Fluent French and conversational English for Paris's international patient base.","Empathetic, patient-centered communication and collaborative clinical mindset."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":8,"hours":5},{"company":"Pinewood Clinics","title":"Pharmacist","description":"Pinewood Clinics is a network of six community family-medicine, physiotherapy, and pharmacy clinics across Île-de-France. We focus on coordinated, unhurried outpatient care backed by shared electronic medical records. We're hiring a Pharmacist to join the team (on-site, Paris, France).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead safe prescription dispensing, clinical medication counseling, and cold-chain inventory management inside Pinewood's integrated clinic pharmacy.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Verify prescriptions for dosage accuracy, drug interactions, and allergies prior to dispensing.\n- Counsel patients clearly on medication administration, side effects, and adherence.\n- Coordinate directly with clinic physicians on substitutions, chronic-care renewals, and vaccine stock.\n- Manage supplier ordering, expiry audits, controlled-substance logs, and cold-chain temperature monitoring.\n- Supervise pharmacy technicians and uphold strict French pharmacy regulatory compliance.\n\nRequirements:\n- Docteur en Pharmacie degree and active registration with the Ordre National des Pharmaciens.\n- 2+ years of retail or clinic pharmacy dispensing experience in France.\n- Fluent French and strong patient-counseling skills.\n- Meticulous habits around inventory controls, regulatory logs, and safety checks.\n\nNice to have:\n- Vaccination administration certification.\n- Experience with French pharmacy dispensing and Carte Vitale billing software.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Mutuelle health coverage and 50% Navigo transit pass reimbursement\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus RTT days per French labor standards\n- Meal vouchers (Tickets Restaurant) and annual clinical training budget\n- Modern, well-equipped treatment rooms with dedicated admin support\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Paris, France","skills":["Pharmacy","Medication Counseling","Inventory Management","Regulatory Compliance"],"reqs":["Docteur en Pharmacie degree and active registration with the Ordre National des Pharmaciens.","2+ years of retail or clinic pharmacy dispensing experience in France.","Fluent French and strong patient-counseling skills.","Meticulous habits around inventory controls, regulatory logs, and safety checks."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":15,"hours":10},{"company":"Pinewood Clinics","title":"Medical Receptionist","description":"Pinewood Clinics is a network of six community family-medicine, physiotherapy, and pharmacy clinics across Île-de-France. We focus on coordinated, unhurried outpatient care backed by shared electronic medical records. We're hiring a Medical Receptionist to join the team (on-site, Paris, France).\n\nAbout the role:\nBe the welcoming face of our Paris clinic on morning or afternoon part-time shifts (24 hrs/week)—keeping patient check-in, Doctolib scheduling, and billing effortless.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Greet arriving patients warmly, verify Carte Vitale / mutuelle details, and manage smooth check-in.\n- Schedule appointments across physicians and physiotherapists via Doctolib and handle phone/email queries.\n- Process co-payments, issue receipts, and handle basic daily till reconciliation.\n- Keep waiting areas tidy and notify clinicians promptly when urgent cases arrive.\n\nRequirements:\n- Fluent French and comfortable conversational English.\n- 1+ year in front-desk hospitality, clinic reception, or customer-facing administration.\n- Warm, calm demeanor during busy clinic hours and strong organizational accuracy.\n- Basic computer literacy and comfort learning medical scheduling software.\n\nNice to have:\n- Prior experience with Doctolib or French medical billing workflows.\n- Additional spoken language (Arabic, Spanish, or Portuguese).\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $650–$1,100 USD / month (Part-time, On-site)\n- Mutuelle health coverage and 50% Navigo transit pass reimbursement\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus RTT days per French labor standards\n- Meal vouchers (Tickets Restaurant) and annual clinical training budget\n- Modern, well-equipped treatment rooms with dedicated admin support\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"junior","type":"part_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Paris, France","skills":["Customer Service","Scheduling","EMR","French","Communication"],"reqs":["Fluent French and comfortable conversational English.","1+ year in front-desk hospitality, clinic reception, or customer-facing administration.","Warm, calm demeanor during busy clinic hours and strong organizational accuracy.","Basic computer literacy and comfort learning medical scheduling software."],"lo":650,"hi":1100,"days":1,"hours":15},{"company":"Pinewood Clinics","title":"Healthcare Data Analyst","description":"Pinewood Clinics is a network of six community family-medicine, physiotherapy, and pharmacy clinics across Île-de-France. We focus on coordinated, unhurried outpatient care backed by shared electronic medical records. We're hiring a Healthcare Data Analyst to join the team (hybrid, Paris, France).\n\nAbout the role:\nAnalyze appointment utilization, patient no-show patterns, and clinical quality indicators across Pinewood's six Paris clinics to support smarter scheduling and care delivery.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Build SQL and Power BI dashboards tracking doctor capacity, wait times, and referral conversion across clinics.\n- Analyze seasonal demand and no-show drivers to optimize booking buffers and reminder cadences.\n- Support clinical directors with anonymized quality-of-care and preventive-screening metrics.\n- Ensure all reporting adheres strictly to GDPR and French health-data privacy (HDS) standards.\n- Present monthly operational insights to clinic managers in clear, non-technical terms.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years of data or operations analysis experience, ideally in healthcare or multi-site services.\n- Strong SQL, Excel, and Power BI (or Tableau) modeling and visualization skills.\n- Solid understanding of statistics and strict patient-data anonymization/privacy habits.\n- Fluent French and English.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with Python/R or clinic EMR/Doctolib analytics exports.\n- Familiarity with GDPR health-data regulations.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Mutuelle health coverage and 50% Navigo transit pass reimbursement\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus RTT days per French labor standards\n- Meal vouchers (Tickets Restaurant) and annual clinical training budget\n- Modern, well-equipped treatment rooms with dedicated admin support\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Paris, France","skills":["SQL","Excel","Power BI","Healthcare Data","Statistics"],"reqs":["2+ years of data or operations analysis experience, ideally in healthcare or multi-site services.","Strong SQL, Excel, and Power BI (or Tableau) modeling and visualization skills.","Solid understanding of statistics and strict patient-data anonymization/privacy habits.","Fluent French and English."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":8,"hours":20},{"company":"Brightpath Academy","title":"Mathematics Teacher","description":"Brightpath Academy is a bilingual K–12 international school serving 950 students in Amman alongside a growing blended online learning division. Our faculty emphasizes inquiry-led STEM, strong literacy foundations, and individualized student mentoring. We're hiring a Mathematics Teacher to join the team (on-site, Amman, Jordan).\n\nAbout the role:\nInspire middle and high school students (Grades 7–10) in Amman through concept-first mathematics instruction, visual problem solving, and differentiated support.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Plan and deliver engaging Grades 7–10 mathematics lessons aligned with international curriculum standards.\n- Design formative quizzes, summative exams, and project-based assessments with timely feedback.\n- Differentiate instruction and run weekly office hours for students needing extra scaffolding or extension.\n- Maintain a calm, respectful classroom culture that encourages mathematical curiosity.\n- Communicate student progress clearly with parents during term reports and conferences.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Mathematics, Mathematics Education, or Engineering plus a teaching credential.\n- 2+ years of full-time secondary mathematics teaching experience.\n- Strong classroom management and ability to explain abstract concepts intuitively.\n- Fluent English instruction skills.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience teaching IB MYP, IGCSE, or US Common Core curricula.\n- Familiarity with GeoGebra, Desmos, or Moodle LMS.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive medical insurance and tuition discount for faculty children\n- Full school-calendar winter and summer breaks plus paid professional development\n- Relocation and housing guidance for international educators\n- Dedicated classroom technology budget and collaborative prep periods\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Education","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Amman, Jordan","skills":["Teaching","Mathematics","Lesson Planning","Classroom Management","Assessment"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Mathematics, Mathematics Education, or Engineering plus a teaching credential.","2+ years of full-time secondary mathematics teaching experience.","Strong classroom management and ability to explain abstract concepts intuitively.","Fluent English instruction skills."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":15,"hours":1},{"company":"Brightpath Academy","title":"English Language Teacher","description":"Brightpath Academy is a bilingual K–12 international school serving 950 students in Amman alongside a growing blended online learning division. Our faculty emphasizes inquiry-led STEM, strong literacy foundations, and individualized student mentoring. We're hiring an English Language Teacher to join the team (on-site, Amman, Jordan).\n\nAbout the role:\nBuild confident readers, writers, and speakers in our 