ith teachers and parents to coordinate individualized support plans.\n- Maintain confidential case notes and uphold school safeguarding protocols.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Psychology, School Counseling, or Social Work.\n- 2+ years of school counseling, youth mentoring, or educational advising experience.\n- Fluent Arabic and English with high empathy, discretion, and safeguarding awareness.\n- Strong knowledge of regional and international university admissions pathways.\n\nNice to have:\n- Certification in adolescent counseling or IB/US university advising.\n- Experience running peer-support or anti-bullying initiatives.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive medical insurance and tuition discount for faculty children\n- Full school-calendar winter and summer breaks plus paid professional development\n- Relocation and housing guidance for international educators\n- Dedicated classroom technology budget and collaborative prep periods\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Education","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Amman, Jordan","skills":["Counseling","Student Support","Communication","Career Guidance","Arabic","English"],"reqs":["Bachelor's or Master's degree in Psychology, School Counseling, or Social Work.","2+ years of school counseling, youth mentoring, or educational advising experience.","Fluent Arabic and English with high empathy, discretion, and safeguarding awareness.","Strong knowledge of regional and international university admissions pathways."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":15,"hours":16},{"company":"Brightpath Academy","title":"Teaching Assistant","description":"Brightpath Academy is a bilingual K–12 international school serving 950 students in Amman alongside a growing blended online learning division. Our faculty emphasizes inquiry-led STEM, strong literacy foundations, and individualized student mentoring. We're hiring a Teaching Assistant to join the team (on-site, Amman, Jordan).\n\nAbout the role:\nSupport primary classroom teachers (20 hrs/week) with small-group literacy/math stations, hands-on activity prep, and individualized student encouragement.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Work alongside lead teachers during lessons to support students in small guided groups.\n- Help prepare classroom materials, visual aids, and hands-on learning stations.\n- Assist with student supervision during transitions, library blocks, and school events.\n- Share helpful observations on student engagement with lead teachers.\n\nRequirements:\n- Currently studying education, psychology, English, or a STEM subject (or recent graduate).\n- Patience, warmth, and genuine enthusiasm for helping children learn.\n- Clear spoken English and Arabic.\n- Reliable morning availability at our Amman campus.\n\nNice to have:\n- Prior tutoring, summer camp, or volunteer classroom experience.\n- Interest in pursuing a full-time teaching career.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $200–$350 USD / month (Part-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive medical insurance and tuition discount for faculty children\n- Full school-calendar winter and summer breaks plus paid professional development\n- Relocation and housing guidance for international educators\n- Dedicated classroom technology budget and collaborative prep periods\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Education","seniority":"intern","type":"part_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Amman, Jordan","skills":["Teaching","Communication","Classroom 