e, On-site)\n- Comprehensive medical insurance and tuition discount for faculty children\n- Full school-calendar winter and summer breaks plus paid professional development\n- Relocation and housing guidance for international educators\n- Dedicated classroom technology budget and collaborative prep periods\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Education","seniority":"lead","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Amman, Jordan","skills":["Teaching","Science","Curriculum Development","Team Leadership","Assessment"],"reqs":["Bachelor's or Master's in a science discipline plus a recognized teaching qualification.","8+ years of secondary science teaching experience, including 2+ years leading a department or grade team.","Demonstrated success raising student outcomes in international exams (IGCSE/IB/AP).","Strong coaching, curriculum-mapping, and lab safety management skills."],"lo":3500,"hi":5200,"days":8,"hours":2},{"company":"Lumen Analytics","title":"Technical Trainer","description":"Lumen Analytics turns fragmented operational and supply-chain data into live forecasting dashboards for mid-market European companies. Our remote-first engineering and data teams serve 140+ B2B customers across logistics, retail, and manufacturing. We're hiring a Technical Trainer to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nRun engaging live remote workshops that help non-technical client ops teams master Lumen dashboards, SQL fundamentals, and self-serve Power BI reporting.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Deliver live, interactive 2-hour to 2-day remote training sessions for enterprise client teams.\n- Author hands-on exercises, cheat sheets, and sandbox datasets tailored to client industries.\n- Adapt pacing and examples smoothly for mixed-skill cohorts (finance, ops, and junior analysts).\n- Collect post-session feedback scores and collaborate with product teams on recurring user confusion.\n- Record crisp 5-minute refresher micro-videos for Lumen's customer academy.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of experience delivering technical software, SQL, or BI training to adult learners.\n- Strong practical fluency in SQL and Power BI (or equivalent BI tools).\n- Engaging presentation presence on video calls and clear, patient instructional style.\n- Portfolio or sample workshop deck/recording you can walk us through.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience designing self-paced LMS courses alongside live workshops.\n- Additional European language (German or French) alongside fluent English.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Contract, Remote)\n- Remote-first setup with a $1,000 home-office hardware grant\n- 28 days paid annual leave and flexible core hours (10:00–15:00 CET overlap)\n- Annual $1,500 personal development and conference budget\n- Annual company-wide offsite and quarterly team meetups\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Education","seniority":"mid","type":"contract","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Training","SQL","Power BI","Presentation","Curriculum Development"],"reqs":["3+ years of experience delivering technical software, SQL, or BI training to adult learners.","Strong practical fluency in SQL and Power BI (or equivalent BI tools).","Engaging presentation presence on video calls and clear, patient instructional style.","Portfolio or sample workshop deck/recording you can walk us through."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":15,"hours":7},{"company":"Atlas Structures","title":"Civil Engineer","description":"Atlas Structures engineers and delivers commercial towers, mixed-use developments, and civil infrastructure projects across Saudi Arabia. With an integrated BIM and site-supervision practice, we manage projects from conceptual structural design through handover. We're hiring a Civil Engineer to join the team (on-site, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia).\n\nAbout the role:\nSupport structural design checks, site inspections, and contractor coordination on commercial mixed-use and civil infrastructure builds in Riyadh.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Review structural shop drawings, reinforcement details, and method statements against design specs.\n- Perform structural calculations and grading/drainage checks using ETABS, SAFE, Civil 3D, and AutoCAD.\n- Conduct daily site walks to verify concrete pours, rebar placement, and formwork quality.\n- Coordinate RFIs, technical submittals, and NCR resolutions with contractors and consultants.\n- Prepare weekly site progress and quality inspection summaries for the Project Manager.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Civil or Structural Engineering (SCE registration eligible).\n- 3+ years of post-graduate experience in commercial building or infrastructure construction.\n- Proficiency in AutoCAD, Civil 3D, and structural analysis tools (ETABS/SAP2000).\n- Strong knowledge of Saudi Building Code (SBC) / ACI / Eurocode standards and site safety.\n\nNice to have:\n- Prior KSA Vision-project or large commercial tower experience.\n- Arabic and English fluency.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Class-A medical insurance for employee and family\n- Annual home-leave airfare allowance and 25 days paid annual leave\n- Site transport/housing allowance for active field assignments\n- Sponsorship for PMP, PE, and Autodesk/BIM certifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Riyadh, Saudi Arabia","skills":["AutoCAD","Structural Analysis","Civil 3D","Site Supervision","Project Management"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Civil or Structural Engineering (SCE registration eligible).","3+ years of post-graduate experience in commercial building or infrastructure construction.","Proficiency in AutoCAD, Civil 3D, and structural analysis tools (ETABS/SAP2000).","Strong knowledge of Saudi Building Code (SBC) / ACI / Eurocode standards and site safety."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":1,"hours":12},{"company":"Atlas Structures","title":"Junior Architect","description":"Atlas Structures engineers and delivers commercial towers, mixed-use developments, and civil infrastructure projects across Saudi Arabia. With an integrated BIM and site-supervision practice, we manage projects from conceptual structural design through handover. We're hiring a Junior Architect to join the team (on-site, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia).\n\nAbout the role:\nTurn conceptual massing studies into coordinated Revit models, permit drawings, and crisp client presentation boards alongside Atlas's senior design architects.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Develop 3D architectural models, floor plans, elevations, and sections in Autodesk Revit and AutoCAD.\n- Produce clean schematic renders and material boards using SketchUp, Lumion/Enscape, and Photoshop.\n- Assist senior architects in coordinating facade, core, and MEP clearances with engineering teams.\n- Assemble permit submission sets and update redline markups accurately.\n- Attend design coordination meetings and document action items.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Architecture with a strong academic or early-career design portfolio.\n- 1+ year of architectural office experience (or substantial studio/internship work).\n- Solid working proficiency in Revit, AutoCAD, and at least one 3D visualization tool.\n- Strong eye for proportion, detailing, and clear drawing standards.\n\nNice to have:\n- Familiarity with Saudi Building Code life-safety and accessibility guidelines.\n- Experience with Rhino or Grasshopper.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Class-A medical insurance for employee and family\n- Annual home-leave airfare allowance and 25 days paid annual leave\n- Site transport/housing allowance for active field assignments\n- Sponsorship for PMP, PE, and Autodesk/BIM certifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Riyadh, Saudi Arabia","skills":["Revit","AutoCAD","SketchUp","Architectural Design","Rendering"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Architecture with a strong academic or early-career design portfolio.","1+ year of architectural office experience (or substantial studio/internship work).","Solid working proficiency in Revit, AutoCAD, and at least one 3D visualization tool.","Strong eye for proportion, detailing, and clear drawing standards."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":8,"hours":17},{"company":"Atlas Structures","title":"Project Manager (Construction)","description":"Atlas Structures engineers and delivers commercial towers, mixed-use developments, and civil infrastructure projects across Saudi Arabia. With an integrated BIM and site-supervision practice, we manage projects from conceptual structural design through handover. We're hiring a Project Manager (Construction) to join the team (on-site, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia).\n\nAbout the role:\nHold end-to-end delivery accountability for a SAR 150M+ commercial development in Riyadh—owning schedule, cost control, subcontractors, and client sign-off.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Lead project execution from mobilization through testing, commissioning, and final handover.\n- Own the master Primavera P6 baseline schedule, critical-path recovery plans, and earned-value tracking.\n- Manage commercial budgets, variation orders, subcontractor payment certificates, and FIDIC contract correspondence.\n- Direct site engineers, QA/QC, and HSE leads to uphold zero-accident and high-quality standards.\n- Chair weekly executive progress meetings with the client, PMC, and lead consultants.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Civil Engineering or Construction Management.\n- 8+ years in commercial construction delivery, including 3+ years as Lead Project Manager.\n- Deep command of Primavera P6, FIDIC contracts, and cost/variation management.\n- Strong leadership presence with GCC site experience.\n\nNice to have:\n- PMP or Chartered Builder (MCIOB) accreditation.\n- Bilingual Arabic and English fluency.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Class-A medical insurance for employee and family\n- Annual home-leave airfare allowance and 25 days paid annual leave\n- Site transport/housing allowance for active field assignments\n- Sponsorship for PMP, PE, and Autodesk/BIM certifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Riyadh, Saudi Arabia","skills":["Project Management","Primavera P6","Budgeting","Contract Management","Team Leadership"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Civil Engineering or Construction Management.","8+ years in commercial construction delivery, including 3+ years as Lead Project Manager.","Deep command of Primavera P6, FIDIC contracts, and cost/variation management.","Strong leadership presence with GCC site experience."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":15,"hours":22},{"company":"Atlas Structures","title":"BIM Coordinator","description":"Atlas Structures engineers and delivers commercial towers, mixed-use developments, and civil infrastructure projects across Saudi Arabia. With an integrated BIM and site-supervision practice, we manage projects from conceptual structural design through handover. We're hiring a BIM Coordinator to join the team (hybrid, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia).\n\nAbout the role:\nKeep architectural, structural, and MEP models clash-free across active Riyadh projects by owning federated model reviews, BIM Execution Plans, and LOD standards.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Federate multidisciplinary Revit models in Navisworks Manage and run weekly clash-detection matrices.\n- Chair interdisciplinary BIM coordination meetings and track clash resolution to closure.\n- Enforce BIM Execution Plan (BEP) naming conventions, shared coordinates, and ISO 19650 workflows.\n- Audit consultant and subcontractor model deliveries for LOD 300–400 compliance.\n- Support quantity take-off exports and 4D schedule visualizations for project controls.\n\nRequirements:\n- Degree in Architecture or Engineering with 3+ years of dedicated BIM coordination experience.\n- Advanced proficiency in Autodesk Revit, Navisworks Manage, and BIM 360 / Autodesk Construction Cloud.\n- Solid understanding of MEP, structural, and architectural constructability clearances.\n- Practical knowledge of ISO 19650 BIM standards.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience automating model checks using Dynamo, Python, or Solibri.\n- Autodesk Certified Professional in Revit.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Class-A medical insurance for employee and family\n- Annual home-leave airfare allowance and 25 days paid annual leave\n- Site transport/housing allowance for active field assignments\n- Sponsorship for PMP, PE, and Autodesk/BIM certifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Riyadh, Saudi Arabia","skills":["BIM","Revit","Navisworks","AutoCAD","Coordination"],"reqs":["Degree in Architecture or Engineering with 3+ years of dedicated BIM coordination experience.","Advanced proficiency in Autodesk Revit, Navisworks Manage, and BIM 360 / Autodesk Construction Cloud.","Solid understanding of MEP, structural, and architectural constructability clearances.","Practical knowledge of ISO 19650 BIM standards."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":1,"hours":3},{"company":"Atlas Structures","title":"Engineering Intern","description":"Atlas Structures engineers and delivers commercial towers, mixed-use developments, and civil infrastructure projects across Saudi Arabia. With an integrated BIM and site-supervision practice, we manage projects from conceptual structural design through handover. We're hiring an Engineering Intern to join the team (on-site, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia).\n\nAbout the role:\nRotate between Atlas's Riyadh design office and active construction sites over 12 weeks—learning quantity take-offs, drawing reviews, and field QA/HSE.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Assist project engineers with quantity take-offs, BOQ checks, and daily site progress logs.\n- Prepare basic AutoCAD redlines and organize submittal/RFI tracking registers in Excel.\n- Shadow QA/QC and HSE engineers during site inspections and toolbox talks.\n- Compile a brief end-of-internship technical learnings presentation.\n\nRequirements:\n- Enrolled in (or recently graduated from) a Civil, Mechanical, or Electrical Engineering program.\n- Basic familiarity with AutoCAD and Microsoft Excel.\n- Willingness to spend time on active construction sites in Riyadh following full PPE rules.\n- Clear communication in English and/or Arabic.\n\nNice to have:\n- Exposure to Revit, Civil 3D, or Primavera P6 in coursework.\n- Valid driver's license.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $450–$800 USD / month (Internship, On-site)\n- Class-A medical insurance for employee and family\n- Annual home-leave airfare allowance and 25 days paid annual leave\n- Site transport/housing allowance for active field assignments\n- Sponsorship for PMP, PE, and Autodesk/BIM certifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Engineering","seniority":"intern","type":"internship","mode":"onsite","location":"Riyadh, Saudi Arabia","skills":["AutoCAD","Excel","Technical Drawing","Communication"],"reqs":["Enrolled in (or recently graduated from) a Civil, Mechanical, or Electrical Engineering program.","Basic familiarity with AutoCAD and Microsoft Excel.","Willingness to spend time on active construction sites in Riyadh following full PPE rules.","Clear communication in English and/or Arabic."],"lo":450,"hi":800,"days":8,"hours":8},{"company":"Meridian Energy","title":"Electrical Engineer","description":"Meridian Energy designs, installs, and maintains rooftop solar PV, battery storage, and energy-efficiency retrofits for warehouses, malls, and commercial campuses across the UAE. We have commissioned over 95 MW of clean commercial capacity. We're hiring an Electrical Engineer to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nEngineer grid-tied commercial rooftop and carport solar PV systems across the UAE—from PVsyst yield modeling and DEWA single-line diagrams to commissioning sign-off.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Design LV/MV electrical layouts, string sizing, cable schedules, and earthing/protection schemes for 200 kWp–5 MWp PV plants.\n- Run energy yield simulations in PVsyst and prepare compliant DEWA/ADDC single-line diagrams.\n- Review switchgear, inverter, and transformer vendor submittals for technical compliance.\n- Support site installation teams during cable pulling, inverter hookup, and cold/hot commissioning tests.\n- Troubleshoot grid-tie protection relays and SCADA telemetry issues.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering.\n- 2+ years of electrical design experience in commercial solar PV or MEP power distribution.\n- Proficiency in AutoCAD, PVsyst, and electrical load/short-circuit calculation tools.\n- Familiarity with IEC solar standards and UAE utility interconnection rules (DEWA Shams / ADDC).\n\nNice to have:\n- DEWA Certified Solar PV Engineer credential.\n- Valid UAE driving license for client site visits.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- UAE medical insurance, life cover, and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Company vehicle or fuel/transport allowance for field and engineering roles\n- Safety gear, specialized tools, and paid DEWA/LEED accreditation support\n- Annual performance bonus tied to commissioned capacity and safety KPIs\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Electrical Design","AutoCAD","Solar PV","Power Systems","Site Supervision"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering.","2+ years of electrical design experience in commercial solar PV or MEP power distribution.","Proficiency in AutoCAD, PVsyst, and electrical load/short-circuit calculation tools.","Familiarity with IEC solar standards and UAE utility interconnection rules (DEWA Shams / ADDC)."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":15,"hours":13},{"company":"Meridian Energy","title":"Solar Installation Technician","description":"Meridian Energy designs, installs, and maintains rooftop solar PV, battery storage, and energy-efficiency retrofits for warehouses, malls, and commercial campuses across the UAE. We have commissioned over 95 MW of clean commercial capacity. We're hiring a Solar Installation Technician to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nJoin our Dubai field crew installing, wiring, and commissioning commercial rooftop and shaded-carport solar arrays to strict safety and workmanship standards.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Install mounting structures, PV modules, DC cable trays, MC4 connectors, and string inverters safely.\n- Perform continuity, insulation resistance (Megger), and open-circuit voltage tests during commissioning.\n- Read electrical single-line and roof-layout drawings accurately on site.\n- Follow strict Lockout/Tagout (LOTO), fall-arrest harness, and heat-stress safety procedures daily.\n- Assist O&M engineers with preventive cleaning, thermal inspections, and inverter fault checks.\n\nRequirements:\n- Technical diploma or vocational certificate in Electrical Installation or Renewable Energy.\n- 1+ year of hands-on electrical or solar PV field installation experience.\n- Comfortable working outdoors and at height on commercial roofs with full PPE.\n- Strong teamwork and zero-shortcuts attitude toward electrical safety.\n\nNice to have:\n- Working at Heights or Basic First Aid / HSE certification.\n- Experience with Huawei, SMA, or Sungrow commercial inverters.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- UAE medical insurance, life cover, and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Company vehicle or fuel/transport allowance for field and engineering roles\n- Safety gear, specialized tools, and paid DEWA/LEED accreditation support\n- Annual performance bonus tied to commissioned capacity and safety KPIs\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Solar PV","Electrical Installation","Safety","Troubleshooting"],"reqs":["Technical diploma or vocational certificate in Electrical Installation or Renewable Energy.","1+ year of hands-on electrical or solar PV field installation experience.","Comfortable working outdoors and at height on commercial roofs with full PPE.","Strong teamwork and zero-shortcuts attitude toward electrical safety."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":1,"hours":18},{"company":"Meridian Energy","title":"Mechanical Engineer (HVAC)","description":"Meridian Energy designs, installs, and maintains rooftop solar PV, battery storage, and energy-efficiency retrofits for warehouses, malls, and commercial campuses across the UAE. We have commissioned over 95 MW of clean commercial capacity. We're hiring a Mechanical Engineer (HVAC) to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead energy-efficiency retrofits for commercial towers and industrial facilities—redesigning chilled-water, VRF, and ventilation systems for major kWh savings.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct on-site HVAC performance audits, thermal load calculations (HAP), and chiller plant assessments.\n- Design energy-efficient HVAC retrofit packages (VFD retrofits, heat-recovery wheels, BMS optimization).\n- Model building energy baselines and projected savings using eQUEST, IESVE, or EnergyPlus.\n- Prepare technical specifications, review contractor submittals, and inspect installations.\n- Verify post-retrofit Measurement & Verification (M&V) savings with operations teams.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Mechanical Engineering.\n- 2+ years of HVAC design, energy retrofits, or district-cooling experience in the GCC.\n- Proficiency in AutoCAD, Carrier HAP, and energy-modeling software.\n- Solid grasp of ASHRAE 90.1/62.1 standards and chilled-water plant hydraulics.\n\nNice to have:\n- CEM (Certified Energy Manager) or CMVP credential.\n- Experience with Building Management Systems (BMS) tuning.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- UAE medical insurance, life cover, and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Company vehicle or fuel/transport allowance for field and engineering roles\n- Safety gear, specialized tools, and paid DEWA/LEED accreditation support\n- Annual performance bonus tied to commissioned capacity and safety KPIs\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["HVAC","AutoCAD","Energy Modeling","Mechanical Design","Site Supervision"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Mechanical Engineering.","2+ years of HVAC design, energy retrofits, or district-cooling experience in the GCC.","Proficiency in AutoCAD, Carrier HAP, and energy-modeling software.","Solid grasp of ASHRAE 90.1/62.1 standards and chilled-water plant hydraulics."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":8,"hours":23},{"company":"Meridian Energy","title":"Sustainability Consultant","description":"Meridian Energy designs, installs, and maintains rooftop solar PV, battery storage, and energy-efficiency retrofits for warehouses, malls, and commercial campuses across the UAE. We have commissioned over 95 MW of clean commercial capacity. We're hiring a Sustainability Consultant to join the team (hybrid, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nAdvise commercial real estate and logistics clients in Dubai on ASHRAE Level 2 energy audits, LEED/Estidama certification, and practical Scope 1–2 decarbonization roadmaps.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Lead ASHRAE Level 1 & 2 energy and water audits across commercial buildings and industrial warehouses.\n- Build financial payback and carbon-abatement models (IRR, NPV, tCO2e) for recommended retrofits.\n- Manage LEED O+M / BD+C documentation submissions and guide project teams through credit compliance.\n- Deliver clear ESG & decarbonization strategy reports and present findings to client executives.\n- Mentor junior engineers on energy-audit data logging and utility-bill normalization.\n\nRequirements:\n- 5+ years in sustainability consulting, energy auditing, or green-building certification.\n- Active LEED AP (BD+C or O+M) or CEM credential.\n- Proven track record leading commercial energy audits and delivering client-ready ROI models.\n- Strong executive communication and report-writing skills in English.\n\nNice to have:\n- Estidama PQP or Al Sa'fat experience in the UAE.\n- Familiarity with GHG Protocol corporate carbon accounting.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Contract, Hybrid)\n- UAE medical insurance, life cover, and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Company vehicle or fuel/transport allowance for field and engineering roles\n- Safety gear, specialized tools, and paid DEWA/LEED accreditation support\n- Annual performance bonus tied to commissioned capacity and safety KPIs\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"senior","type":"contract","mode":"hybrid","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Sustainability","Energy Auditing","LEED","Reporting","Client Management"],"reqs":["5+ years in sustainability consulting, energy auditing, or green-building certification.","Active LEED AP (BD+C or O+M) or CEM credential.","Proven track record leading commercial energy audits and delivering client-ready ROI models.","Strong executive communication and report-writing skills in English."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":15,"hours":4},{"company":"Meridian Energy","title":"Operations Coordinator","description":"Meridian Energy designs, installs, and maintains rooftop solar PV, battery storage, and energy-efficiency retrofits for warehouses, malls, and commercial campuses across the UAE. We have commissioned over 95 MW of clean commercial capacity. We're hiring an Operations Coordinator to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nKeep Meridian's Dubai installation crews, solar equipment warehouse, and client site schedules moving smoothly without parts delays or idle truck rolls.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Coordinate weekly site schedules for 4 installation crews, crane/lift bookings, and gate-pass permits.\n- Track solar panel, inverter, and racking stock levels in our warehouse and raise purchase orders on time.\n- Match supplier packing lists against project BOMs and flag shortages before crew mobilization.\n- Send proactive timeline updates to client facility managers ahead of site visits.\n- Maintain clean job-costing and delivery-note folders in Excel and ERP.\n\nRequirements:\n- 1+ year in operations coordination, supply chain, or construction/field-service scheduling.\n- Strong Excel skills (formulas, schedules, inventory tracking) and high attention to detail.\n- Clear, proactive English communication by phone and email.\n- Organized problem-solver who stays calm when site plans shift.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience in MEP, solar, or UAE logistics/warehouse coordination.\n- Conversational Arabic or Hindi/Urdu for coordinating field crews.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- UAE medical insurance, life cover, and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Company vehicle or fuel/transport allowance for field and engineering roles\n- Safety gear, specialized tools, and paid DEWA/LEED accreditation support\n- Annual performance bonus tied to commissioned capacity and safety KPIs\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Scheduling","Excel","Procurement","Communication","Inventory Management"],"reqs":["1+ year in operations coordination, supply chain, or construction/field-service scheduling.","Strong Excel skills (formulas, schedules, inventory tracking) and high attention to detail.","Clear, proactive English communication by phone and email.","Organized problem-solver who stays calm when site plans shift."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":1,"hours":9},{"company":"Cedar Labs","title":"Engineering Manager","description":"Cedar Labs builds web, mobile, and dispatch software for retail and last-mile logistics teams across the Levant and Gulf. Founded by product engineers in Beirut, our 35-person team ships weekly releases directly with store operators and fleet coordinators. We're hiring an Engineering Manager to join the team (hybrid, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead a 6-engineer full-stack and mobile squad at Cedar Labs—balancing technical architecture guidance, people growth, hiring, and predictable product delivery.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Manage, coach, and run regular 1:1s and growth plans for 6 frontend, backend, and mobile engineers.\n- Own engineering execution, sprint predictability, and production quality across two core logistics products.\n- Partner with Product and Design leads to scope quarterly roadmaps and resolve technical trade-offs early.\n- Lead technical hiring—refining take-home/pairing rubrics and closing senior and mid-level talent.\n- Stay close enough to the code to review critical system designs, RFCs