cts from discovery interviews to shipped design systems. We're hiring a Design Lead to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nSet the craft bar across Northwind's 8-person remote design team—directing client strategy, coaching designers in critiques, and stewarding studio-wide quality.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Oversee design quality and UX strategy across 4–6 concurrent startup client engagements.\n- Mentor mid and junior designers through structured weekly critiques and career check-ins.\n- Lead high-stakes kickoff workshops and executive design reviews with startup founders and VPs.\n- Evolve Northwind's reusable Figma starter kits, accessibility checklists, and handoff standards.\n- Partner with studio founders on project scoping, proposals, and design hiring.\n\nRequirements:\n- 8+ years in digital product design, including 2+ years managing or leading product designers.\n- An exceptional portfolio spanning zero-to-one startup launches and mature design systems.\n- Deep Figma craft, systems thinking, and strong written/spoken storytelling.\n- Experience thriving in an asynchronous, remote-first studio environment.\n\nNice to have:\n- Prior agency/studio leadership or founding designer experience.\n- Familiarity with front-end engineering workflows (React/Tailwind/Motion).\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $4,500–$6,800 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- 100% remote async-friendly culture with 4-day summer Fridays\n- 25 days paid leave plus end-of-year studio closure\n- $1,000/year Figma, research tools, and design conference stipend\n- Monthly wellness and coworking pass reimbursement\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Design","seniority":"lead","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Design Leadership","Figma","Design Systems","UX Strategy","Mentoring"],"reqs":["8+ years in digital product design, including 2+ years managing or leading product designers.","An exceptional portfolio spanning zero-to-one startup launches and mature design systems.","Deep Figma craft, systems thinking, and strong written/spoken storytelling.","Experience thriving in an asynchronous, remote-first studio environment."],"lo":4500,"hi":6800,"days":15,"hours":19},{"company":"Harbor Finance","title":"Tax Consultant","description":"Harbor Finance provides fractional CFO advisory, statutory audit, tax structuring, and cross-border accounting for high-growth SMEs in the UK and Europe. Our advisory squads combine chartered accountants with modern cloud finance tooling. We're hiring a Tax Consultant to join the team (hybrid, London, UK).\n\nAbout the role:\nAdvise Harbor's UK SME clients on corporation tax computations, R&D tax credits, VAT structuring, and HMRC compliance from our London Bridge office.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Prepare and review UK corporate tax computations (CT600) and complex VAT returns.\n- Advise fast-growing client founders on R&D tax relief claims, EMI share schemes, and cross-border VAT.\n- Respond to HMRC inquiries clearly and manage statutory filing deadlines across client portfolios.\n- Identify proactive tax efficiencies during year-end reviews and group restructurings.\n- Stay current on UK Finance Act updates and share concise briefings with advisory teams.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years in UK corporate tax and VAT advisory within an accounting practice.\n- ATT, CTA, ACA, or ACCA qualification (or advanced CTA finalist).\n- Strong technical command of UK corporation tax, VAT rules, and tax-preparation software.\n- Clear, commercial client communication—able to explain tax rules without jargon.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience preparing R&D tax credit narratives or SEIS/EIS filings.\n- Familiarity with Alphatax or CCH Tax.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Full study support and paid exam leave for ACCA, ACA, or CPA\n- 25 days paid holiday plus UK bank holidays and hybrid travel card\n- Private medical and dental cover plus pension matching\n- Flexible hybrid schedule (2–3 days/week in our London Bridge office)\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Finance","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"London, UK","skills":["Tax","VAT","Corporate Tax","Excel","Compliance","Client Management"],"reqs":["3+ years in UK corporate tax and VAT advisory within an accounting practice.","ATT, CTA, ACA, or ACCA qualification (or advanced CTA finalist).","Strong technical command of UK corporation tax, VAT rules, and tax-preparation software.","Clear, commercial client communication—able to explain tax rules without jargon."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":1,"hours":0},{"company":"Mediterra Health","title":"Clinical Pharmacist","description":"Mediterra Health operates three multidisciplinary outpatient clinics, an accredited diagnostic lab, and a 24/7 bilingual telehealth platform. Over 80 clinicians collaborate across primary care, chronic disease management, and preventive screenings. We're hiring a Clinical Pharmacist to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nEmbed directly with Mediterra's internal medicine and cardiology physicians in Beirut to optimize chronic-care regimens, antimicrobial stewardship, and medication safety.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct comprehensive medication therapy management (MTM) reviews for polypharmacy and chronic-care patients.\n- Round with physicians to advise on renal dosing adjustments, drug–drug interactions, and formulary choices.\n- Lead clinic-wide medication-safety audits, high-alert drug protocols, and adverse-event reporting.\n- Deliver structured training sessions on safe prescribing and administration to nursing staff.\n- Counsel complex patients on anticoagulation, diabetes, and respiratory inhaler regimens.\n\nRequirements:\n- PharmD or Master's in Clinical Pharmacy plus an active Lebanese Order of Pharmacists license.\n- 5+ years of hospital or clinical ambulatory-care pharmacy experience.\n- Strong command of evidence-based clinical guidelines (ESC, ADA, IDSA) and EMR documentation.\n- Fluent Arabic and English with strong interprofessional collaboration.\n\nNice to have:\n- PGY1/PGY2 pharmacy residency or Board Certified Pharmacotherapy Specialist (BCPS).\n- Experience in outpatient anticoagulation or heart-failure clinics.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,400–$3,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive medical coverage and discounted family care at all clinics\n- Paid CME (Continuing Medical Education) days and conference support\n- Malpractice coverage and structured shift scheduling without surprise double-shifts\n- 20 days paid annual leave plus public holidays\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Clinical Pharmacy","Medication Review","Patient Counseling","EMR","Guidelines"],"reqs":["PharmD or Master's in Clinical Pharmacy plus an active Lebanese Order of Pharmacists license.","5+ years of hospital or clinical ambulatory-care pharmacy experience.","Strong command of evidence-based clinical guidelines (ESC, ADA, IDSA) and EMR documentation.","Fluent Arabic and English with strong interprofessional collaboration."],"lo":2400,"hi":3800,"days":8,"hours":5},{"company":"Saffron Kitchens","title":"Brand Designer","description":"Saffron Kitchens operates 18 neighborhood restaurants alongside a high-volume direct delivery app serving 25,000+ weekly orders. We combine hospitality craft with modern kitchen operations, CRM retention, and real-time order logistics. We're hiring a Brand Designer to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nShape the tactile and digital look of Saffron Kitchens—from eco-friendly delivery boxes and seasonal dine-in menus to store signage and app promos.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Design packaging dielines, stickers, bags, and print menus that make delivery orders feel memorable.\n- Maintain visual consistency across 18 restaurant interiors, digital menu boards, and ordering app banners.\n- Art-direct food photography shoots alongside our culinary and social teams.\n- Prepare accurate print-ready artwork and coordinate directly with packaging printers on proofs.\n- Evolve our brand guidelines as new sub-brands and seasonal concepts launch.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of brand, packaging, or hospitality visual design experience.\n- Portfolio showcasing tactile packaging work, editorial menus, and strong typography.\n- Expert proficiency in Adobe Illustrator, Photoshop, InDesign, and Figma.\n- Working knowledge of print substrates, spot colors, and packaging production.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience designing Arabic–English bilingual packaging and signage.\n- Food styling or photography direction experience.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Medical coverage and daily staff meal allowance across all locations\n- 18 days paid annual leave plus paid sick and family leave\n- Monthly dining credit across all Saffron Kitchens brands\n- Structured career progression across corporate and store leadership\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Design","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Branding","Adobe Illustrator","Packaging Design","Typography","Figma"],"reqs":["3+ years of brand, packaging, or hospitality visual design experience.","Portfolio showcasing tactile packaging work, editorial menus, and strong typography.","Expert proficiency in Adobe Illustrator, Photoshop, InDesign, and Figma.","Working knowledge of print substrates, spot colors, and packaging production."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":15,"hours":10},{"company":"Kite Payments","title":"Customer Success Manager","description":"Kite Payments runs card acquiring, payout orchestration, and fraud screening infrastructure for over 4,000 online merchants across the GCC. Regulated and security-first, we process high-volume multi-currency transactions with sub-second checkout latency. We're hiring a Customer Success Manager to join the team (hybrid, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nOwn post-sale onboarding, checkout conversion health, and expansion for Kite's highest-volume e-commerce and marketplace merchants across the UAE.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Guide newly signed merchants from KYB approval through sandbox testing and live checkout launch.\n- Run quarterly business reviews (QBRs) analyzing payment approval rates, chargebacks, and local payment adoption.\n- Identify upsell opportunities (Apple Pay, Tabby/Tamara integrations, multi-currency payouts) to grow NRR.\n- Coordinate closely with Risk, Tech Support, and Product teams to resolve merchant blockers fast.\n- Capture structured merchant feedback to influence Kite's quarterly product roadmap.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years in B2B customer success, account management, or partner operations (ideally in SaaS or fintech).\n- Strong relationship-building skills and comfort discussing technical APIs or checkout metrics.\n- Proficiency with CRM tools (HubSpot/Salesforce) and structured account health tracking.\n- Fluent English; Arabic fluency is a major plus for regional merchants.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience in payments, e-commerce platforms (Shopify/Magento), or MENA fintech.\n- Track record managing a portfolio exceeding $1M+ ARR/GMV equivalents.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Comprehensive UAE medical insurance for employee and dependents\n- Annual flight ticket allowance and 22 days paid annual leave\n- Performance bonus tied to company reliability and growth milestones\n- Relocation support for candidates moving to Dubai\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Marketing","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Customer Success","CRM","Communication","Onboarding","Account Management"],"reqs":["2+ years in B2B customer success, account management, or partner operations (ideally in SaaS or fintech).","Strong relationship-building skills and comfort discussing technical APIs or checkout metrics.","Proficiency with CRM tools (HubSpot/Salesforce) and structured account health tracking.","Fluent English; Arabic fluency is a major plus for regional merchants."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":1,"hours":15}]$seed$::jsonb) as x(
    company text, title text, description text, field text, seniority text, type text, mode text,
    location text, skills text[], reqs text[], lo int, hi int, days int, hours int)
),
upd_j as (
  update public.jobs e
  set
    description = j.description,
    requirements = j.reqs,
    skills = j.skills,
    field = j.field,
    seniority = j.seniority::public.seniority,
    employment_type = j.type::public.employment_type,
    work_mode = j.mode::public.work_mode,
    location = j.location,
    salary_min = j.lo,
    salary_max = j.hi,
    salary_currency = 'USD'
  from src_j j
  join all_c c on c.name = j.company
  where e.is_demo and e.company_id = c.id and e.title = j.title
  returning e.id
)
insert into public.jobs (company_id, title, description, requirements, skills, field, seniority, employment_type, work_mode, location, salary_min, salary_max, salary_currency, status, is_demo, published_at)
select
  c.id,
  j.title,
  j.description,
  j.reqs,
  j.skills,
  j.field,
  j.seniority::public.seniority,
  j.type::public.employment_type,
  j.mode::public.work_mode,
  j.location,
  j.lo,
  j.hi,
  'USD',
  'open'::public.job_status,
  true,
  now() - make_interval(days => j.days, hours => j.hours)
from src_j j
join all_c c on c.name = j.company
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.jobs e join public.companies ec on ec.id = e.company_id
  where e.is_demo and ec.name = j.company and e.title = j.title
);
